# What goes into the release archive (git archive / the GitHub release zip that Zenodo stores with the DOI).
#
# Policy: the archive is the reproducible record of the research, so it keeps everything that code, tests, data,
# article scripts or documentation use: tests and their meshes, examples, utdata/, r/, the website sources and the
# CI workflows. Only files that nothing uses and that carry no research content are marked export-ignore here. When in
# doubt, a file stays in the archive. Check what is left out with:
#   git -c core.quotepath=off ls-files | sort | comm -13 <(git archive HEAD | tar -t | sort) -

# A byte-identical copy of web/public/vitki_logo.jpg under the app's earlier name; no page or script refers to it.

# Generated by uv pip compile (see its header); collapsed in GitHub diffs
requirements.lock linguist-generated=true

